      "content": "Pruning specific weight clusters to discern specialized intuition from general physics knowledge can be challenging without exact human-like understanding. Generally, clusters contributing to general knowledge may be more connected to fundamental interactions, while specialized layers may be more focused and narrower in scope. You can start by examining the activations of each layer when being exposed to the most representative input and remove layers that show minimal changes in activation when comparing the specialized and general cases. This heuristic can be iteratively refined by cross-relating activations with known outcomes and progressively settling on clusters with consistent impact across various general test cases while minimally affecting the specialized prediction. It's an empirical trial and error process with room for systematic refinement.",
